---
import ApiTable from '../../components/ApiTable.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Demo from '../../components/Demo.astro';
import Heading from '../../components/Heading.astro';
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';

const demo = `<lm-card variant="stop">
  <p class="lm-kicker">Stop 2 of 6 · 2018 to 2021</p>
  <h2>Front-end developer, Example Co.</h2>
  <p>Frontend with some backend on example.com and example.org.</p>
</lm-card>
<lm-card variant="pass">
  <p class="lm-kicker">Boarding pass</p>
  <h2>Wheels up</h2>
  <p>Pass variant: tighter padding for a display title.</p>
</lm-card>`;
// Built from a constant: a literal triple dash inside frontmatter confuses parsers.
const fence = '-'.repeat(3);
const astro = `${fence}
import '@luismatute/ui/components/card';
import '@luismatute/ui/base.css';
${fence}
<lm-card variant="pass">
  <h1>Wheels up</h1>
</lm-card>`;
const css = `/* lm-card reads these tokens; override them on the element */
lm-card {
  --lm-card: var(--lm-cream);
  --lm-shadow-card: none;
}`;
const toc = [
  { id: 'demo', label: 'Live demo' },
  { id: 'usage', label: 'Usage' },
  { id: 'in-astro', label: 'In Astro' },
  { id: 'attributes', label: 'Attributes' },
  { id: 'custom-properties', label: 'CSS custom properties' },
  { id: 'events', label: 'Events' },
  { id: 'accessibility', label: 'Accessibility' },
  { id: 'reduced-motion', label: 'Reduced motion' },
];
---

<Docs
  slug="components/lm-card"
  title="lm-card"
  description="A paper ticket with a hard ink shadow. A plain container: put any heading and copy inside."
  toc={toc}
  extraCss="components.css"
>
  <Heading id="demo">Live demo</Heading>
  <Demo name="lm-card" label="lm-card, stop and pass variants" code={demo}>
    <div class="demo-row">
      <lm-card variant="stop">
        <p class="lm-kicker">Stop 2 of 6 · 2018 to 2021</p>
        <h2>Front-end developer, Example Co.</h2>
        <p>Frontend with some backend on example.com and example.org.</p>
      </lm-card>
      <lm-card variant="pass">
        <p class="lm-kicker">Boarding pass</p>
        <h2>Wheels up</h2>
        <p>Pass variant: tighter padding for a display title.</p>
      </lm-card>
    </div>
  </Demo>
  <Heading id="usage">Usage</Heading>
  <p>Import the element and <code>base.css</code> once, then use it anywhere. It follows day and night through the tokens. The demo's markup is above.</p>
  <Heading id="in-astro" level={3}>In Astro</Heading>
  <p>The component subpath registers the element as a side effect.</p>
  <CodeBlock lang="astro" filename="Card.astro" code={astro} />
  <Heading id="attributes">Attributes</Heading>
  <ApiTable
    caption="lm-card attributes"
    head={['Attribute', 'Description']}
    rows={[{ name: 'variant', detail: '<code>stop</code> (default, set on connect) or <code>pass</code>, which tightens the padding and styles an <code>h1</code> as the display title.' }]}
  />
  <Heading id="custom-properties">CSS custom properties</Heading>
  <p>The card reads these tokens. Override them on the element or a parent.</p>
  <ApiTable
    caption="lm-card custom properties"
    head={['Property', 'Used for']}
    rows={[
      { name: '--lm-card', detail: 'Background. Paper by day, deep brown at night.' },
      { name: '--lm-ink', detail: 'Text and the thick border.' },
      { name: '--lm-shadow-card', detail: 'The hard offset shadow.' },
      { name: '--lm-radius-card', detail: 'Corner radius (20px).' },
      { name: '--lm-rule-route', detail: 'Dashed rules around a <code>.lm-route</code> list.' },
    ]}
  />
  <CodeBlock lang="css" filename="site.css" code={css} />
  <Heading id="events">Events</Heading>
  <p>None. <code>lm-card</code> is a styled container.</p>
  <Heading id="accessibility">Accessibility</Heading>
  <ul>
    <li>No role is added: use a real heading inside so the card shows up in the page outline.</li>
    <li>Ink on card colour is over 12:1 in both modes.</li>
  </ul>
  <Heading id="reduced-motion">Reduced motion</Heading>
  <p>The card doesn't animate.</p>
</Docs>
